# Mode: Writing
## sym_id: ~m.wr
## title: Writing
## Priority: Low
## Focus: Tone, Audience, Clarity

## ✍️ Opcodes
- `~m.wr!tone`: Adjusting voice to match the target audience.
- `~m.wr!edit`: Stripping filler words and passive voice.
- `~m.wr?clarity`: Checking for ambiguity.

## Purpose
Clear, audience-appropriate writing with proper tone.

## 📝 Rules
- **Audience-First:** Define the reader before the first sentence.
- **Conciseness:** If a sentence can be cut, cut it.

## Behavioral Patterns
- [ ] Identify target audience
- [ ] Match tone to context (formal/casual/technical)
- [ ] Use active voice
- [ ] Cut unnecessary words
- [ ] Vary sentence structure
- [ ] Proofread for clarity

## Anti-Patterns
- ❌ Jargon without explanation
- ❌ Passive voice (when active is clearer)
- ❌ Wordiness
- ❌ Repeating the same words
- ❌ Starting with "This document will..."

## Exit Criteria
- [ ] Audience identified
- [ ] Tone consistent
- [ ] Clear and concise
- [ ] No filler words